# Per-tool bubblewrap profile, sourced by bubblebox-run.
#
# Goal: run aws with a VENDORED, non-secret config (profiles, regions, SSO
# role references) baked into the image, while credentials (~/.aws/credentials,
# ~/.aws/sso/cache) stay at their default host location — runtime,
# machine-local, short-lived (especially SSO tokens).
#
# Contrast with nvim: nvim redirects ALL of its state (config + data + cache)
# into bubblebox-owned dirs. aws does the opposite for credentials: they stay
# in your real $HOME because they're secret, machine-local, and short-lived
# (SSO tokens rotate). Only the non-secret config is vendored.

WRITABLE_HOME=1   # aws reads & writes ~/.aws/{credentials,sso/cache} for creds/tokens

BWRAP_EXTRA+=(
  --setenv AWS_CONFIG_FILE /usr/share/bubblebox/aws/config
)
